lisa-design:
- Two phases: each updater Scans pins into Refs, Decide plans them against targets, ApplyAll rewrites only the planned Changes. Dry runs, conflict reports and PR bodies all come from the same plan.
- Never downgrade: semver-newer pins and pseudo-versions whose commit time is after the target tag's commit are Conflicts and are left as they are. A pin that is not a version (alpine:3.20, branch, SHA, "latest") is replaced; shared-workflow refs are replaced whenever they differ from the given ref (no semver check), since @v1 vs @v1.2.0 isn't a downgrade.
- Internal = any github.com/compliance-framework/<repo> module, in or outside the manifest (mock plugins also pin the product agent module; its releases are only read). Only direct go.mod requires are bumped; indirect ones follow via go mod tidy.
- Edits are in-place regexp/line edits, not YAML re-serialisation, so comments and layout survive; values that are not versions (opa-version: ${{ ... }}) are not matched.
- Dockerfile/ui/opa updaters are only enabled for repos of kind action/ui/policies, with their source repo taken from the manifest's depends_on (the caller fills Config).
- Mock-specific knowledge is limited to the ui sync script table: scripts/sync-mock-api-version.sh records its tag in src/api-version.json (current version); the real ui script has no recorded version, so its current version is unknown.
- Split into a 3-PR stack for the 1000-line limit: (1) core + updaters, (2) helm updater + GitHub client, (3) cmd/ccf-bump, ccf-bump-sync.yml, docs.
